    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d246">

                <pb facs="0328" n="235" sameAs="frus:frus1935v04/pg235"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">714.18/33: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Minister in Costa Rica</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Sack</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic"
                        >to the Secretary of State</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps">San
                                José</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1935-02-28T11:00:00-06:00">February 28, 1935—11
                        a.m.</date><lb/>[Received 1:50 p.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>10. The following telegram has been sent to Guatemala: <quote rend="blockquote">
                        <p>“February 28, 10 a.m. Your telegram of February 27, 4 p.m.<anchor n="4"
                                xml:id="d246-f1"/> Because of age and condition of his health
                            Ricardo Fernandez Guardia withdrew acceptance yesterday of mission to
                            Guatemala and the Minister of Foreign Affairs consequently requests the
                            date for exchange of telegrams be changed to March 5th to permit him to
                            arrange for appointment of another Minister.</p>
                        <p>The Government here has understood that requests for <hi
                                rendition="#italic">agrément</hi> of Ministers would be made
                            simultaneously, neither party referring to a previous request received
                            from the other, in order to avoid the impression that either Government
                            was taking the initiative. The Minister for Foreign Affairs therefore
                            suggests that both telegrams be filed at the same hour on the morning of
                            March 5 and contain no reference to a request for <hi
                                rendition="#italic">agrément</hi> received from the other
                            Government. Telegrams extending <hi rendition="#italic">agrément</hi>
                            can be exchanged subsequently.</p>
                        <p>Repeated to the Department.”</p>
                    </quote></p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sack</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
